{"id":"u-c813ee75-e5a8-42b4-8170-4245e4057c0c","src":"community","title":"Black Swordsman","author":"Anonymous","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/R8Oxhy-black-swordsman","desc":"Description generated by AI.\n\nBlack Swordsman is a 15-week Power Hypertrophy Upper Lower (PHUL)-style 4-day split designed for intermediate lifters who want to build serious upper body strength and size without neglecting lower body maintenance. The program runs on a 4-week loading block followed by a deload week, cycling three times across the 15 weeks.\n\nDay 1 (Upper Power) focuses on heavy compound movements — Bench Press, Bent Over Row, Overhead Press, and Weighted Pull-Ups — all trained at RPE 9 in the 3-5 rep range to maximize strength adaptation. Accessory work follows with Skull Crushers and Bicep Curls to reinforce the arms without excessive fatigue.\n\nDay 2 (Lower Power) keeps leg volume intentional but not excessive. Hack Squat and Romanian Deadlift are trained heavy, followed by Leg Curl, Seated Calf Raise, and Abs to maintain lower body strength and function.\n\nDay 3 (Upper Hypertrophy) shifts to moderate loads and higher reps for muscle growth. Incline Bench Press and Cable Fly develop the chest, Single Arm Iso Row and Front Pulldown build back thickness, and Lateral Raise plus Rear Delt Fly ensure full shoulder development including the often neglected rear delts.\n\nDay 4 (Lower Hypertrophy + Arms) is the lightest day — isolation focused. Single Leg Extension and Leg Curl maintain quad and hamstring size, while Lateral Raise, Hammer Curl, Preacher Curl, Tricep Rope Pushdown, and Reverse Bicep Curl round out arm and delt development including forearm work.\n\nThis program is ideal for lifters who are naturally strong in the lower body and want to prioritize upper body aesthetics and strength, while still training legs with enough volume to maintain and slowly progress.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"join